PM — status board

File: openOODA/PM.oot
DESIGN is the want. SHIPPED is what exists. SPRINT is this week. This file is the pin.

Release: v0.198.0-alpha
Product tip (ooda): main
Boards tip: main
Std tip: main
Beta is not the current release.

Rebuild: PURE_NO_ARC=0. Memory is freed when the last use drops.
You do not need wasmtime, clang, or a special env file for the native path.

Words
  The compiler works for the core product.
  Residual means wanted, not built. Not forbidden.

Status words
  done — works, proved
  smoke — small check passes
  partial — part works
  residual — wanted, not built
  open — this week

Open work: SPRINT.oot (empty this week)
What exists: SHIPPED.oot
What we want: DESIGN.oot
Scripts: ../ooda/scripts/*_smoke.oo
Honesty packs: ../ooda/bootstrap/*.oot
Std today: 50 .oo files under ../ooda/std. About 561 under org std/.

How to re-prove
  cd ../ooda
  export PURE_NO_ARC=0 PURE_SKIP_CHECK=1
  OODAC_BIN=./bootstrap/seed/oodac bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build oodac/main.oo oodac/oodac
  OODAC_BIN=./oodac/oodac bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build oodac/main.oo oodac/oodac
  ./oodac/oodac check oodac/main.oo
  Expect OK. Last live run here was about 25 seconds and about 0.32 GiB.

CI honesty
  `oodac check scripts/ci_product.oo` only typechecks those rails.
  It does not emit, gcc, or run them.
  Official rebuild is `bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build`.
